{
 "version": 1,
 "contract": "AC-1 revision 4",
 "about": "Section 3.11 \"Header safety\" (I12, R3-M8). mailbox: a strict RFC 5321 Mailbox: ASCII dot-atom local part (atext and dots, no dot first, last or doubled, 1 to 64 bytes), one @, a domain of 2 or more labels of letters, digits and hyphens (1 to 63 bytes, no hyphen first or last; xn-- A-labels are checked as LDH only), no trailing dot, at most 254 bytes; anything else is bad-mailbox. header: every configured field and subject argument; a value holding U+0000 to U+001F, U+007F to U+009F, U+2028 or U+2029 is refused (code bad-mailbox for mailbox fields, null otherwise). fold: printable ASCII header text as \"Name: text\"; while a line is over 78 characters it breaks before the last space at index 78 or less (never the space right after \"Name:\"), else before the first space after, else the line stays whole; the space starts the next line; lines joined with CRLF. encoded_words: any other text as RFC 2047 \"=?UTF-8?B?<base64 with padding>?=\" words of whole characters, greedy, each word at most 75 characters and its line at most 78 (the first line includes \"Name: \"), joined with CRLF and a space. qp: the body with \\n line breaks to quoted-printable: bytes 33 to 126 except = literal, space and tab literal except as a hard line's last byte, every other byte =XX upper-case; before a token that would make the line longer than 75, the line ends with a soft break \"=\"; lines joined with CRLF, ending with CRLF. dot_stuff: a \".\" at the start of the data or right after CRLF gets one more (a bare LF starts no line). graph_path: the Graph sendMail mailbox as one path segment, every UTF-8 byte outside RFC 3986 unreserved percent-encoded upper-case. subjects: the 8.4 subjects filled with args, as the Subject header.",
